#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""ccburn: live burn-rate dashboard for Claude Code, Codex and Antigravity spend.

Reads the Claude Code and Codex CLIs' own on-disk transcripts (scan/price/
de-dupe pipeline ported from t3code `apps/server/src/usage/`) and the
conversation databases of Antigravity, Google's agent for the Gemini models,
prices them against LiteLLM's rate table, and redraws one screen: trailing 5/15/60 min
rates with an end-of-day projection, today's total, per-provider and per-model
tables, and a per-minute stacked chart of the last hour.

Costs are API-equivalent estimates, not what a subscription bills.

Extra Claude Code config dirs (one per profile), Codex homes and Antigravity
data dirs go in ~/.config/ccburn/config.json, see config.example.json.
"""

